rvation knowledge","building pathology","traditional materials","measured survey","Revit/HBIM","GIS","photogrammetry","heritage documentation","site experience"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning is not simply “architect who restores old buildings.” A modern Conservation Architect should combine heritage knowledge, architectural design, scientific documentation, and digital technologies."},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Architecture"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Architectural History"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Building Conservation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Traditional Materials"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Digital Documentation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"HBIM / GIS"},{"text":"+"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Adaptive Reuse","CONSERVATION ARCHITECT","Heritage Specialist","Conservation Consultant","Heritage / Digital Heritage Architect"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best graduate profile:"},{"type":"p","text":"Conservation Architect specializing in historic-building documentation, heritage assessment, restoration, adaptive reuse, and digital heritage technologies such as HBIM, GIS, photogrammetry, and 3D scanning."},{"type":"flow","items":["generally B.Arch","specialized M.Arch/PG program in Architectural Conservation or Heritage Conservation","field-based conservation experience","senior conservation/heritage consultancy roles"],"label":"For a student targeting this career seriously, the strongest route is"}]}]}